WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.010
After indulging themselves to their hearts' content, the girls concluded the Christmas feast as they always did

2
00:00:07.011 --> 00:00:10.558
—with a cup of hot tea and words of affection from Mother.

3
00:00:10.559 --> 00:00:14.930
"This has been a trying year for all of us," Mother said.

4
00:00:14.931 --> 00:00:21.730
"So thank you, my little daughters, for gracefully yet courageously bearing our burdens."

5
00:00:21.731 --> 00:00:28.382
Because of everything that had happened that day, the girls had been unable to present their gift to Mother.

6
00:00:28.383 --> 00:00:31.405
Therefore they were planning to give it to her now.

7
00:00:31.406 --> 00:00:37.165
"Mother, we have something for you," said Jo as she signaled Amy with her eyes.

8
00:00:37.166 --> 00:00:41.831
Amy, meanwhile, was tugging and yanking at a knot in her curls.

9
00:00:41.832 --> 00:00:51.531
"I shouldn't have allowed those children to touch my hair," Amy complained, recalling the two little Hummel girls who had played with her beloved hair.

10
00:00:51.532 --> 00:00:58.112
"Amy!" Jo barked sharply, as she tilted her head to indicate the box hidden behind her.

11
00:00:58.113 --> 00:01:02.209
The girls had agreed that the youngest should bestow the gift.

12
00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:07.373
"Oh!" Amy flushed as she stood to carry out her duty.

13
00:01:07.374 --> 00:01:17.380
Mother delicately took out the gifts one by one without uttering a sound, yet her eyes conveyed the depth of love and appreciation she felt for her girls.

14
00:01:17.381 --> 00:01:23.969
Clutching each gift tenderly, she simply said: "My little women."

15
00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:29.353
Bright and early the next morning, Jo slipped upstairs to her sanctuary in the attic.

16
00:01:29.354 --> 00:01:36.830
There she had pushed an old oak desk near the oval window, along with a shaky chair and large wicker basket.

17
00:01:36.831 --> 00:01:41.413
That basket housed what Jo the writer called "the dregs."

18
00:01:41.414 --> 00:01:46.407
All her incomplete, meaningless, and undesirable thoughts were discarded there.

19
00:01:46.408 --> 00:01:51.169
The family knew better than to disturb Jo when she was in her creative mode.

20
00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:56.786
Those foolish or fearless enough might encounter one of Jo's infamous temper tantrums.

21
00:01:56.787 --> 00:02:03.964
Meg, at this moment, chose to take that risk, as she charged in, waving a card in her hand.

22
00:02:03.965 --> 00:02:07.621
"Jo! You'll never believe what this is!" Meg cried.

23
00:02:07.622 --> 00:02:12.119
Jo crumpled the paper she had been writing on and tossed it into the dregs.

24
00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:16.703
"If you don't tell me soon, that is going to end up in there!"

25
00:02:16.704 --> 00:02:24.971
Jo said menacingly as she pointed a threatening finger at the paper in Meg's hand and kicked the wastebasket with her foot.

26
00:02:24.972 --> 00:02:31.366
"The Gardiners have invited us to a New Year's ball!" Meg could hardly contain her excitement.

27
00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:37.115
"A ball?" Jo shrieked. "Who cares about some stupid ball?"

28
00:02:37.116 --> 00:02:44.904
Meg narrowed her eyes and said in a cool tone: "I do. How else are you going to meet your future husband?"

29
00:02:44.905 --> 00:02:50.569
It took all of Jo's might to restrain herself from losing her temper.

30
00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:57.531
"There are more important things in life, Meg, than to be married," Jo replied in a calm voice.

31
00:02:57.532 --> 00:03:02.650
"Well, I want to go," said Meg, ignoring Jo's growls and grumbles.

32
00:03:02.651 --> 00:03:08.655
"And Mother says I may," she paused, "only if we both go."

33
00:03:08.656 --> 00:03:12.878
Meg finally looked at Jo with an almost desperate gaze.

34
00:03:12.879 --> 00:03:19.323
Immediately Jo's stubborn heart softened at her sister's silent plea.

35
00:03:19.324 --> 00:03:24.159
To Jo's dismay, the day of the ball arrived more quickly than she expected.

36
00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:30.743
Although she was secretly praying for a severe snowstorm or some other incident that would force the ball to be canceled,

37
00:03:30.744 --> 00:03:35.024
outwardly Jo put on her happy face and got ready for the event.

38
00:03:35.025 --> 00:03:37.445
"What gloves will you wear with your dress?"

39
00:03:37.446 --> 00:03:41.132
Meg glanced at Jo's maroon frock hanging on the door.

40
00:03:41.133 --> 00:03:44.636
"I don't have any," was Jo's curt reply.

41
00:03:44.637 --> 00:03:47.767
"You must wear gloves," Meg insisted.

42
00:03:47.768 --> 00:03:52.767
"Gloves are so . . . so . . . silly!" Jo blurted out.

43
00:03:52.768 --> 00:03:57.868
"A true lady must wear gloves," Meg said, her voice rising.

44
00:03:57.869 --> 00:04:02.269
Jo bit her lip to stop herself from saying something nasty to Meg.

45
00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:08.132
Instead, rolling her eyes, Jo said: "Then I'll just have to borrow a pair of yours."

46
00:04:08.133 --> 00:04:15.777
"Absolutely not," was Meg's curt reply. "Look at your big hands. You'll stretch mine out."

47
00:04:15.778 --> 00:04:19.581
Like all mothers, Mrs. March had a good sense of timing.

48
00:04:19.582 --> 00:04:26.140
At that instant, she waltzed in with a pair of her own gloves, preventing another one of Jo's explosions.

49
00:04:26.141 --> 00:04:31.396
"I thought you might need these." Mother smiled as she handed Jo the gloves.

50
00:04:31.397 --> 00:04:38.315
Finally, after more shrill cries and minor mishaps, the girls were ready for the ball.

51
00:04:38.316 --> 00:04:44.055
"You both look beautiful," praised Beth when she saw her sisters in their ball dresses.

52
00:04:44.056 --> 00:04:51.168
"Like two princesses! Just remember to find a handsome prince!" giggled Amy.

53
00:04:51.169 --> 00:04:55.967
The Gardiners were a wealthy family who often entertained guests at their mansion.

54
00:04:55.968 --> 00:05:06.208
Sallie Gardiner was Meg's good friend. The young girls knew each other since childhood and remained close friends even after Meg's father lost his fortune.

55
00:05:06.209 --> 00:05:15.904
"Isn't this sublime, Jo?" Meg called out happily as she and her dancing partner glided past Jo, who sat tugging her tight dress collar.

56
00:05:15.905 --> 00:05:22.904
"Lovely," mumbled Jo. She looked longingly outside at a group of young men kicking a ball around.

57
00:05:22.905 --> 00:05:31.116
It was so unfair. Jo hated living by rules that told her young women had to look pretty, giggle, and be ladylike.

58
00:05:31.117 --> 00:05:34.917
Meanwhile, boys could do as they please.

59
00:05:34.918 --> 00:05:38.255
"Why can't I do that?" she said aloud.

60
00:05:38.256 --> 00:05:41.542
"Do what?" a voice asked from behind.

61
00:05:41.543 --> 00:05:46.035
Jo whipped her head around and came face to face with the Laurence boy.

62
00:05:46.036 --> 00:05:50.776
"That's very rude of you," she scolded, wagging a finger at him.

63
00:05:50.777 --> 00:05:53.752
"What is?" he retorted.

64
00:05:53.753 --> 00:06:02.791
"Creeping up behind a lady and frightening her out of her wits," Jo said, dramatically placing a gloved hand over her forehead.

65
00:06:02.792 --> 00:06:12.501
"I beg your pardon." The young man bowed deeply then continued: "Then I shall leave the lady to her wits."

66
00:06:12.502 --> 00:06:19.536
"Wait!" Jo called out. "You can stay as long as you don't bore me like this party."

67
00:06:19.537 --> 00:06:24.749
"So you don't like balls?" the Laurence boy asked with a twinkle in his eye.

68
00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:28.657
"I can't stand them. Look at those silly girls.

69
00:06:28.658 --> 00:06:37.886
Their dresses are so tight, it's a wonder they're still breathing!" Jo tugged her collar again, reminding herself of her own discomfort.

70
00:06:37.887 --> 00:06:42.559
"I don't fancy these sorts of things either," replied the young man.

71
00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:45.534
"What are you doing here then?" asked Jo.

72
00:06:45.535 --> 00:06:49.959
"My grandfather made me come," he replied, frowning.

73
00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:53.769
"Oh, which reminds me," Jo exclaimed suddenly.

74
00:06:53.770 --> 00:06:56.697
"Thank you for the lovely Christmas meal."

75
00:06:56.698 --> 00:07:02.844
The Laurence boy shrugged and said casually: "Grandfather sent it, not me."

76
00:07:02.845 --> 00:07:09.277
Jo elbowed him in a very unladylike manner and said: "But I know it was you who told him."

77
00:07:09.278 --> 00:07:13.139
"Do you have a name?" he asked, his cheeks flushing.

78
00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:15.400
"Jo," she replied.

79
00:07:15.401 --> 00:07:18.963
"That's not a very girlish name," he pointed out.

80
00:07:18.964 --> 00:07:25.214
"It's short for Josephine. But if you call me that, I won't ever speak to you again."

81
00:07:25.215 --> 00:07:29.439
Laughing, he said: "I'm Laurie."

82
00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:33.192
Jo's loud laugh caused many people to glance their way.

83
00:07:33.193 --> 00:07:41.350
"What kind of a name is Laurie Laurence?" she said, struggling to resist bursting out in laughter again.

84
00:07:41.351 --> 00:07:43.715
Laurie pretended to be offended.

85
00:07:43.716 --> 00:07:48.581
"My real name is Theodore but I prefer to be called Laurie.

86
00:07:48.582 --> 00:07:58.175
If you have a problem with that," he paused, adding with a wicked glint in his eyes, "Josephine, then I won't ever speak to you again either."

87
00:07:58.176 --> 00:08:02.279
Jo punched him playfully and let out another hearty laugh.

88
00:08:02.280 --> 00:08:10.047
Nearby, people shook their heads and commented on that ill-mannered, noisy young woman.

